{\*\bkmkstart _Toc481496607}How to compile the example sources{\*\bkmkend _Toc481496607}
\par }\pard\plain \qj\widctlpar\adjustright \f1\fs22\cgrid {This is an evaluation copy of the IPION virtual physics engine. The distribution includes the IPION virtual physics link library "ivp_lib.lib" (which 
provides the actual physical simulation), a simple graphics link library "graph_lib.lib" (which is based on DirectX 6.0) and a lot of different quickstart and more sophisticated example sources (on how to use the physics library).
\par Note: The following suffixes may be added to the library names:
\par 
\par {\pntext\pard\plain\f3\fs22\lang1033\cgrid \loch\af3\dbch\af0\hich\f3 \'b7\tab}}\pard \qj\fi-360\li360\widctlpar\jclisttab\tx360{\*\pn \pnlvlblt\ilvl0\ls88\pnrnot0\pnf3\pnstart1\pnindent360\pnhang{\pntxtb \'b7}}\ls88\adjustright {_eval\tab \tab \tab 
