\par {\*\bkmkstart _Toc481496608}{\listtext\pard\plain\s2 \b\f1\fs36\lang1033\cgrid \hich\af1\dbch\af0\loch\f1 4.1\tab}}\pard\plain \s2\fi-864\li864\sb480\sa360\keepn\widctlpar\jclisttab\tx576\tqr\tx864\ls47\ilvl1\outlinelevel1\adjustright \b\f1\fs36\cgrid {
The simpliest way to compile the supplied example sources{\*\bkmkend _Toc481496608}
\par }\pard\plain \qj\widctlpar\adjustright \f1\fs22\cgrid {Just doubleclick the file 'examples_using_graphlib.dsw' (MicroSoft Visual C++ 6.0 must be installed).
\par 
\par Choose 'Rebuild all' from menu 'Build'.
\par 
\par To start the example executable you can optionally specify the following parameters:
\par 
\par {\pntext\pard\plain\f14\fs22\lang1033\cgrid \loch\af14\dbch\af0\hich\f14 \'a7\tab}}\pard \qj\fi-360\li360\widctlpar\jclisttab\tx360{\*\pn \pnlvlblt\ilvl0\ls56\pnrnot0\pnf14\pnstart1\pnindent360\pnhang{\pntxtb \'a7}}\ls56\adjustright {
-example <name> (where <name> is the example's name; e.g. 'snowflake')
\par {\pntext\pard\plain\f14\fs22\lang1033\cgrid \loch\af14\dbch\af0\hich\f14 \'a7\tab}}\pard \qj\fi-360\li360\widctlpar\jclisttab\tx360{\*\pn \pnlvlblt\ilvl0\ls56\pnrnot0\pnf14\pnstart1\pnindent360\pnhang{\pntxtb \'a7}}\ls56\adjustright {
-libpath <path> (where <path> is the correct path to the Ipion 'IVP_Sample_Data' directory; can be omitted if directory 'IVP_Sample_Data' is present in your working directory)
\par }\pard \qj\widctlpar\adjustright {
\par Omitting the '-example' parameter will start the standard IPION demo (as found on the website).
\par 
\par 
\par 
\par {\*\bkmkstart _Toc481496609}{\listtext\pard\plain\s2 \b\f1\fs36\lang1033\cgrid \hich\af1\dbch\af0\loch\f1 4.2\tab}}\pard\plain \s2\fi-864\li864\sb480\sa360\keepn\widctlpar\jclisttab\tx576\tqr\tx864\ls47\ilvl1\outlinelevel1\adjustright \b\f1\fs36\cgrid {
How to compile custom example sources{\*\bkmkend _Toc481496609}
\par }\pard\plain \qj\widctlpar\adjustright \f1\fs22\cgrid {There are two ways to compile an IPION example source:
\par {\pntext\pard\plain\f14\fs22\lang1033\cgrid \loch\af14\dbch\af0\hich\f14 \'a7\tab}}\pard \qj\fi-360\li360\widctlpar\jclisttab\tx360{\*\pn \pnlvlblt\ilvl0\ls57\pnrnot0\pnf14\pnstart1\pnindent360\pnhang{\pntxtb \'a7}}\ls57\adjustright {as a WIN32 console ap
plication without graphical output
\par {\pntext\pard\plain\f14\fs22\lang1033\cgrid \loch\af14\dbch\af0\hich\f14 \'a7\tab}}\pard \qj\fi-360\li360\widctlpar\jclisttab\tx360{\*\pn \pnlvlblt\ilvl0\ls57\pnrnot0\pnf14\pnstart1\pnindent360\pnhang{\pntxtb \'a7}}\ls57\adjustright {
as a WIN32 application with graphical output (using the IPION graph_lib link library)
\par }\pard \qj\widctlpar\adjustright {
\par 
\par {\listtext\pard\plain\s3 \b\f1\fs28\lang1033\cgrid \hich\af1\dbch\af0\loch\f1 4.2.1\tab}}\pard\plain \s3\qj\fi-864\li864\sb480\sa120\keepn\widctlpar\jclisttab\tx720\tqr\tx864\ls47\ilvl2\outlinelevel2\adjustright \b\f1\fs28\cgrid {
Compiling as WIN32 DirectX console application
\par }\pard\plain \qj\widctlpar\adjustright \f1\fs22\cgrid {Open the 'IVP_Sample_Sources' directory and create a new example source file (best to use one of the existing source files as template).
\par 
\par Create a new MicroSoft Visual C++ 6.0 project. Make sure to choose a WIN32 console application and leave it empty. After the project has successfully been created, manually add your example source file and the files 'IVP_Sample_Sources\\
ive_example_common.cxx' and 'IVP_Sample_Sources\\ive_nogfx.cxx' to your project.
\par 
\par There are some changes that need to be applied to the project's settings:
\par {\pntext\pard\plain\f14\fs22\lang1033\cgrid \loch\af14\dbch\af0\hich\f14 \'a7\tab}}\pard \qj\fi-360\li360\widctlpar\jclisttab\tx360{\*\pn \pnlvlblt\ilvl0\ls58\pnrnot0\pnf14\pnstart1\pnindent360\pnhang{\pntxtb \'a7}}\ls58\adjustright {
add '/I "IVP_Include"' to "Project options" on the "C/C++" page
\par {\pntext\pard\plain\f14\fs22\lang1033\cgrid \loch\af14\dbch\af0\hich\f14 \'a7\tab}}\pard \qj\fi-360\li360\widctlpar\jclisttab\tx360{\*\pn \pnlvlblt\ilvl0\ls58\pnrnot0\pnf14\pnstart1\pnindent360\pnhang{\pntxtb \'a7}}\ls58\adjustright {
add "DEBUG" to "Preprocessor definitions" on the "C/C++" page if you want to compile the source in debug mode
\par {\pntext\pard\plain\f14\fs22\lang1033\cgrid \loch\af14\dbch\af0\hich\f14 \'a7\tab}}\pard \qj\fi-360\li360\widctlpar\jclisttab\tx360{\*\pn \pnlvlblt\ilvl0\ls58\pnrnot0\pnf14\pnstart1\pnindent360\pnhang{\pntxtb \'a7}}\ls58\adjustright {
add "NDEBUG" to "Preprocessor definitions" on the "C/C++" page if you want to compile the source in release mode
\par {\pntext\pard\plain\f14\fs22\lang1033\cgrid \loch\af14\dbch\af0\hich\f14 \'a7\tab}}\pard \qj\fi-360\li360\widctlpar\jclisttab\tx360{\*\pn \pnlvlblt\ilvl0\ls58\pnrnot0\pnf14\pnstart1\pnindent360\pnhang{\pntxtb \'a7}}\ls58\adjustright {
add the following files to the "Object/library modules" on the "Link" page: "winmm.lib" \line "ivp_lib.lib"
\par }\pard \qj\widctlpar\adjustright {
\par Use 'Rebuild all' to compile the example source. The resulting executable can either be started from within the developer studio or from the desktop/shell by simply invoking it by its name (i.e. no additional parameters needed).
\par 
\par 
\par {\listtext\pard\plain\s3 \b\f1\fs28\lang1033\cgrid \hich\af1\dbch\af0\loch\f1 4.2.2\tab}}\pard\plain \s3\qj\fi-864\li864\sb480\sa120\keepn\widctlpar\jclisttab\tx720\tqr\tx864\ls47\ilvl2\outlinelevel2\adjustright \b\f1\fs28\cgrid {
Compiling as WIN32 application
\par }\pard\plain \qj\widctlpar\adjustright \f1\fs22\cgrid {
\par Open the 'IVP_Sample_Sources' directory and create a new example source file (best to use one of the existing source files as template).
\par 
\par Create a new MicroSoft Visual C++ 6.0 project. Make sure to choose a WIN32 application and leave it empty. After the project has successfully been created, manually add your example source file and the file 'IVP_Sample_Sources\\
ive_example_common.cxx' to your project.
\par 
\par There are some changes that need to be applied to the project's settings:
\par {\pntext\pard\plain\f14\fs22\lang1033\cgrid \loch\af14\dbch\af0\hich\f14 \'a7\tab}}\pard \qj\fi-360\li360\widctlpar\jclisttab\tx360{\*\pn \pnlvlblt\ilvl0\ls59\pnrnot0\pnf14\pnstart1\pnindent360\pnhang{\pntxtb \'a7}}\ls59\adjustright {
add '/I "IVP_Include"' to "Project options" on the "C/C++" page
\par {\pntext\pard\plain\f14\fs22\lang1033\cgrid \loch\af14\dbch\af0\hich\f14 \'a7\tab}}\pard \qj\fi-360\li360\widctlpar\jclisttab\tx360{\*\pn \pnlvlblt\ilvl0\ls59\pnrnot0\pnf14\pnstart1\pnindent360\pnhang{\pntxtb \'a7}}\ls59\adjustright {
add "DEBUG" to "Preprocessor definitions" on the "C/C++" page if you want to compile the source in debug mode
\par {\pntext\pard\plain\f14\fs22\lang1033\cgrid \loch\af14\dbch\af0\hich\f14 \'a7\tab}}\pard \qj\fi-360\li360\widctlpar\jclisttab\tx360{\*\pn \pnlvlblt\ilvl0\ls59\pnrnot0\pnf14\pnstart1\pnindent360\pnhang{\pntxtb \'a7}}\ls59\adjustright {
add "NDEBUG" to "Preprocessor definitions" on the "C/C++" page if you want to compile the source in release mode
\par {\pntext\pard\plain\f14\fs22\lang1033\cgrid \loch\af14\dbch\af0\hich\f14 \'a7\tab}}\pard \qj\fi-360\li360\widctlpar\jclisttab\tx360{\*\pn \pnlvlblt\ilvl0\ls59\pnrnot0\pnf14\pnstart1\pnindent360\pnhang{\pntxtb \'a7}}\ls59\adjustright {
add the following files to the "Object/library modules" on the "Link" page:\line "dinput.lib"\line "dxguid.lib" \line "dsound.lib"  \line "d3drm.lib" \line "ddraw.lib" \line "winmm.lib" \line "ivp_lib.lib" \line "graph_lib.lib" 
\par }\pard \qj\widctlpar\adjustright {
\par When creating a new example supply an individual name for it to be registered with the graph_lib's main loop (see variable "my_name" in example constructor).
\par 
\par Use 'Rebuild all' to compile the example source. The resulting executable can either be started from within the developer studio or from the desktop/shell.
\par 
\par To start the executable specify the following parameters:
\par 
\par {\pntext\pard\plain\f14\fs22\lang1033\cgrid \loch\af14\dbch\af0\hich\f14 \'a7\tab}}\pard \qj\fi-360\li360\widctlpar\jclisttab\tx360{\*\pn \pnlvlblt\ilvl0\ls60\pnrnot0\pnf14\pnstart1\pnindent360\pnhang{\pntxtb \'a7}}\ls60\adjustright {
example <name> (where <name> is the example's name; e.g. 'snowflake')
\par {\pntext\pard\plain\f14\fs22\lang1033\cgrid \loch\af14\dbch\af0\hich\f14 \'a7\tab}}\pard \qj\fi-360\li360\widctlpar\jclisttab\tx360{\*\pn \pnlvlblt\ilvl0\ls60\pnrnot0\pnf14\pnstart1\pnindent360\pnhang{\pntxtb \'a7}}\ls60\adjustright {
libpath <path> (where <path> is the correct path to the Ipion 'IVP_Sample_Data' directory; can be omitted if directory 'IVP_Sample_Data' is present in your working directory)
\par }\pard \qj\widctlpar\adjustright {
\par Omitting the '-example' parameter will start the standard IPION demo (as found on the website).
\par }\pard\plain \s20\qj\widctlpar\adjustright \f2\fs22\cgrid {
