What is that RotMot anyway?
\par }\pard\plain \qj\widctlpar\adjustright \f1\fs22\cgrid {A RotMot (rotation motor) works just like a real motor. It has a certain power which leads to a certain rotation force.  Ju
st like with a car having an automatic gear this torque gets lower with higher rotation speed. Parameters are: power, maximum force to be applied, maximum rotation speed.
\par {\listtext\pard\plain\s3 \b\f1\fs28\lang1033\cgrid \hich\af1\dbch\af0\loch\f1 5.8.2\tab}}\pard\plain \s3\qj\fi-864\li864\sb480\sa120\keepn\widctlpar\jclisttab\tx720\tqr\tx864\ls47\ilvl2\outlinelevel2\adjustright \b\f1\fs28\cgrid {Creating anchors
\par }\pard\plain \qj\widctlpar\adjustright \f1\fs22\cgrid {We need two anchors for a rotmot: these two points define an a
xis (within our virtual world) around which the object will rotate. Please note that this axis only defines the orientation of the rotation axis, and not the position! The object will always rotate around its mass-center. On how to create anchors please s
ee previous Quickstart tutorial.
\par {\listtext\pard\plain\s3 \b\f1\fs28\lang1033\cgrid \hich\af1\dbch\af0\loch\f1 5.8.3\tab}}\pard\plain \s3\qj\fi-864\li864\sb480\sa120\keepn\widctlpar\jclisttab\tx720\tqr\tx864\ls47\ilvl2\outlinelevel2\adjustright \b\f1\fs28\cgrid {Creating the rotmot

\par }\pard\plain \qj\widctlpar\adjustright \f1\fs22\cgrid {All we need to do to create a rotmot is to fill in a }{\i IVP_Template_Rot_Mot}{ template (include }{\i ivp_templates.hxx}{
). We only have to set the necessary values and  to-be-used anchors. Here is some example code:
\par 
\par }\pard\plain \s17\li288\widctlpar\tx851\tx1418\tx1985\tx2552\tx3119\tx3686\tx4253\tx4820\adjustright \f2\fs22\cgrid {IVP_Template_Rot_Mot rmt;
\par }\pard\plain \qj\fi284\widctlpar\adjustright \f1\fs22\cgrid {\f2\cgrid0 rmt.max_rotation_speed = 40.0;
\par rmt.power              = 4.0;
\par rmt.max_torque         = 3.8;
\par }\pard\plain \s17\li288\widctlpar\tx851\tx1418\tx1985\tx2552\tx3119\tx3686\tx4253\tx4820\adjustright \f2\fs22\cgrid {
\par rmt.anchors[0] = left_anchor_template;
\par rmt.anchors[1] = right_anchor_template;
\par environment->create_rotmot(&rmt);
\par }\pard\plain \qj\widctlpar\adjustright \f1\fs22\cgrid {
