\par {\listtext\pard\plain\s3 \b\f1\fs28\lang1033\cgrid \hich\af1\dbch\af0\loch\f1 5.12.3\tab}}\pard\plain \s3\qj\fi-864\li864\sb480\sa120\keepn\widctlpar\jclisttab\tx720\tqr\tx864\ls47\ilvl2\outlinelevel2\adjustright \b\f1\fs28\cgrid {
Object collision listener
\par }\pard\plain \qj\widctlpar\adjustright \f1\fs22\cgrid {If you want to be notified whenever an object collides with another object you might subclass }{\i IVP_Listener_Collision}{ (include }{\i ivp_listener_collision.hxx}{
). This class provides one single callback-method:
\par event_collision: will be called whenever the corresponding object collides with another object
\par Here is some example code:
\par 
\par }\pard\plain \s17\li288\widctlpar\tx851\tx1418\tx1985\tx2552\tx3119\tx3686\tx4253\tx4820\adjustright \f2\fs22\cgrid {\fs20 class Example_Callback_Listener_Collision : public IVP_Listener_Collision
\par \{
