\par There are two main aspects to each physical object: collision topology (IVP_SurfaceManager and IVP_Compact_Surface) and physical behaviour (IVP_Real_Object and IVP_Core).
\par 
\par Ipion utilizes a very object-orientated concept (quite similar to classes in e.g. C++) when dealing with physical objects. Each object has got a base object (a so-called \ldblquote compact surface\rdblquote 
,  IVP_Compact_Surface), describing its topolgy (i.e. its shape). Multiple physical objects can share a compact surfac
e (there's no limit), but each  physical object can only have one single compact surface. Each physical object has got one individual physical core, describing its physical values (e.g. mass, rotation dampening, etc.).
\par 
\par There are two different kind of physical objects (depending on their shape):
