e surface of a polygon. The IVP_Surface_Manager_Polygon adds some functionality to this raw data and provides an interface to the IVP_Real_Object classes.
\par }\pard\plain \qj\widctlpar\adjustright \f1\fs22\cgrid {
\par A compact surface describes the 3-dimensional topology (shape) of a  concave/convex object. The comp
act surface consists of one or more convex sub-surfaces, so-called 'ledges' ( IVP_Compact_Ledge ). Thus the compact surface of an already convex object (e.g. a cube) simply contains one single ledge while a concave (e.g. an L-shaped) object would contain 
at least two ledges. See below 2-dimensional illustration. 
\par 
