\par }\pard\plain \qj\widctlpar\adjustright \f1\fs22\cgrid {Active Values (Floats/Ints) are simple objects used to store a single value (Note: This chapter will concentrate on }{\i IVP_U_Active_Float}{s, }{\i IVP_U_Active_Int}{
s work accordingly). This value can be the result of a complex calculation, normally dependent of other active floats. In this case the value is calculated when one of the base Active_Floats is changed, not when the value is needed (push policy). 
\par So the value of an Active Float is always valid, no further calculation needed, allowing for getting it very efficiently (inline function). 
\par IVP_U_Active_Float_Listeners may register to listen to every value change of an active value:
